  "verbalization": "Vitetrifolin D is shown to interact with the proteasome subunit beta type-2 and ARO, both of which are targets of a complex, structurally similar compound. This suggests that Vitetrifolin D may exert its effects through a common mechanism, possibly by inhibiting a shared target or modulating a shared pathway. The evidence indicates that Vitetrifolin D may act on a protein involved in cellular degradation, as both the proteasome subunit beta type-2 and ARO are targets of the same compound. The presence of BJ as a target in both pathways implies that Vitetrifolin D may influence cellular processes related to protein homeostasis or degradation, potentially leading to downstream effects on cellular function. The high scores in the final_score suggest that the relationship between Vitetrifolin D and BJ is supported by strong mechanistic evidence, though further validation would be needed to confirm the exact role of BJ in this context.",
